\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Multi-stage trace synthesis. Generation (provider family A) runs a ground-truth-directed LangGraph loop with real tool execution and the tiered perturbation hook; staged verification (deliberately a \emph  {different} provider family) combines a strict clinical pass with a repair-and-re-verify loop; a dual-gate leak audit and corpus assembly produce the frozen canonical release; the audit bars are measured counts. The verifier's 92 first-pass rejections span three categories --- the third (uncorrected spatial drift) exists only because the perturbation mechanism creates genuine judgment pressure.}}{11}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:multistage}{{7}{11}{Multi-stage trace synthesis. Generation (provider family A) runs a ground-truth-directed LangGraph loop with real tool execution and the tiered perturbation hook; staged verification (deliberately a \emph {different} provider family) combines a strict clinical pass with a repair-and-re-verify loop; a dual-gate leak audit and corpus assembly produce the frozen canonical release; the audit bars are measured counts. The verifier's 92 first-pass rejections span three categories --- the third (uncorrected spatial drift) exists only because the perturbation mechanism creates genuine judgment pressure}{figure.caption.14}{}}
\newlabel{fig:multistage@cref}{{[figure][7][]7}{[1][10][]11}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Corpus composition (measured from the released trace files). Five cohorts --- three findings-bearing, two healthy negative controls --- exist in two exact arms (with-tools and no-tools) with per-cohort 1:1 parity; the with-tools corpus carries 5{,}144 finding-level annotations (4{,}513 unique: the 202-image Tufts overlap cohort is contained in the 280-image Tufts all-diseases cohort, so its findings are counted in both). Class mix of the unique findings below; the teacher surveys every finding on an image, and healthy scans carry empty finding sets.}}{12}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:corpus}{{8}{12}{Corpus composition (measured from the released trace files). Five cohorts --- three findings-bearing, two healthy negative controls --- exist in two exact arms (with-tools and no-tools) with per-cohort 1:1 parity; the with-tools corpus carries 5{,}144 finding-level annotations (4{,}513 unique: the 202-image Tufts overlap cohort is contained in the 280-image Tufts all-diseases cohort, so its findings are counted in both). Class mix of the unique findings below; the teacher surveys every finding on an image, and healthy scans carry empty finding sets}{figure.caption.15}{}}
\newlabel{fig:corpus@cref}{{[figure][8][]8}{[1][10][]12}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The verified corpus, regenerated from the released trace files. With-tools and no-tools cohorts are in exact 1:1 parity (checkmarks). Turns and tool calls are for the with-tools side; findings are counted per cohort (the Tufts overlap cohort is a subset of the Tufts all-diseases cohort, so its findings are counted in both).}}{12}{table.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:corpus}{{2}{12}{The verified corpus, regenerated from the released trace files. With-tools and no-tools cohorts are in exact 1:1 parity (checkmarks). Turns and tool calls are for the with-tools side; findings are counted per cohort (the Tufts overlap cohort is a subset of the Tufts all-diseases cohort, so its findings are counted in both)}{table.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{tab:corpus@cref}{{[table][2][]2}{[1][11][]12}{}{}{}}
